          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Another Peek Beyond the Point"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.087,
            0.625,
            0.109
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is 0.039 m in centimetres and millimetres?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.113,
            0.847,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "By looking at these divisions, we can frame a simple rule for dividing decimals by 1, 10, 100, 1000, and so on."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.151,
            0.847,
            0.208
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When we divide a decimal by 1, 10, 100, 1000, and so on, we can just move the decimal point to the left by as many places as there are zeroes in the divisor!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.218,
            0.844,
            0.457
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.154,
                0.218,
                0.844,
                0.457
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_8_table_4.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Decimal</td><td>÷ 10</td><td>÷ 100</td><td>÷ 1000</td><td>÷ 10000</td></tr><tr><td>18.7</td><td>1.87</td><td>0.187</td><td>0.0187</td><td>0.00187</td></tr><tr><td>21.1</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>0.13</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td>2.146</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>0.0058</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.477,
            0.847,
            0.499
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 7: Neenu has 29 metres of red ribbon and wants to share it"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.498,
            0.578,
            0.537
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "equally with Anu. What is the length of ribbon that each of them will get?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.541,
            0.577,
            0.6
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since the ribbon needs to be divided into two equal parts, each girl will get a piece of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 9 \\div 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " metres."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.605,
            0.577,
            0.68
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If each of them gets 14 m, then 1 m remains. If we divide 1 m among the two, each will get another "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 2 }   \\mathrm { m }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.688,
            0.515,
            0.725
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How do we convert "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " into a decimal?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.728,
            0.578,
            0.812
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It is easy to express a fraction as a decimal if the denominator is 1, 10, 100, 1000, etc. So, can we find a fraction equivalent to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " with such a denominator?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.66,
            0.506,
            0.856,
            0.611
          ],
          "content": [
